sprig, the Rust port (harness/sprig-rs)
Copyright the openDaisugi contributors.

It is part of openDaisugi and is MIT licensed. It builds on these crates
from crates.io, each used under one of the licences it offers:

  rustls           Apache-2.0 OR ISC OR MIT (the API backend's https)
  ring             Apache-2.0 AND ISC (rustls's crypto; carries C and
                   assembly code, compiled by its build script, with
                   getrandom, once_cell, cfg-if and libc, MIT OR
                   Apache-2.0)
  rustls-pki-types MIT OR Apache-2.0
  rustls-webpki    ISC
  untrusted        ISC
  subtle           BSD-3-Clause
  zeroize          Apache-2.0 OR MIT

The crates that only run at build time (cc, shlex, find-msvc-tools) are
not in the binary. The Rust standard library (MIT OR Apache-2.0, used
under Apache-2.0, Copyright the Rust Project Developers) is linked into
the binary. The exact crate versions are in harness/sprig-rs/Cargo.lock,
and harness/sprig-rs/PINS.md says why each one is there.

src/goerr.rs carries three tables printed by the Go standard library
(Go 1.25.12, linux/amd64): the errno texts of syscall.Errno, the signal
names of syscall.Signal, and the code points strconv.IsPrint calls not
printable. They are used under the Go licence:

